{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475038-my-character-s-mothley-think-he-is-a-loyalist","id":1475038,"title":"My character's mothley think he is a loyalist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-20T06:54:28-08:00","id":1475038,"title":"My character's mothley think he is a loyalist","content":"I'm playing a game of Changeling The Lost, and my character is pretty screwed up lol. As a player myself and my friends are enjoying it a lot, but our characters are not as lucky.<br /> <br /> My character is a beast of the spring court, a playmate. His duration in Arcadia was not unpleasant, in fact, it was even pleasurable! He was a pampered and well cared for pet, and the only real effort he had to make was to learn tricks to keep the Keeper happy with him. He doesn't want to go back to Arcadia, but he doesn't have the negative stigma other Changelings have towards fairies, so he had no problem making a deal with a fairy in exchange for a favor. The problem, he enjoys wandering the Hedge, so after getting caught in the thorns, he forgot the favor he had done for the fairy, remembering only that a Fairy owed him a favor.<br /> <br /> So, one of his friends got lost in the hedge while we were being chased by giant insects. My character, worried about her, decided to invoke the favor of the fairy so that she would return her friend safe and sound.<br /> <br /> The problem? now all the mothley believes that he is a loyalist. He never complained about his life in Arcadia, and even admitted that he enjoyed it, and now, he summoned a True Fae (which is pretty strong evidence in my opinion). As a last sign of trust, they asked him what favor he had done for the fairy, and my character did not know how to answer them. That gave them even more indication that he is a loyalist.<br /> <br /> After that, my character risked his life for one of his companions (the same one that suspected of him in the first place) and his companion believed that he had done it so he could return her to her Keepet than out of genuine concern.<br /> <br /> Has anyone had an experience like this? It's a very fun thing to play, even if my character doesn't think the same, heheh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27221-maddie","name":"Maddie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T13:33:46-08:00","id":1475144,"title":"","content":"The game collapsed pretty quickly, but I had a character sort of like that. A fairest who was 'married' to her keeper. It was an abusive relationship, sure. But she was literally alone and on the street, then magically whisked away to opulence.<br /> <br /> The thing was, she never ran from her keeper. Her keeper was basically tricked by another gentry into breaking a name oath, killing them - she ran before she could be taken as a 'prize'. She actually wants to AVENGE her keeper. Part of her arc would have been to acknowledge the abuse, and what her keeper really saw her for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T14:15:49-08:00","id":1475148,"title":"","content":"I've had fun in similar situations too, but Oaths tend to make sure the situation doesn't get too out of hand. Oaths are a big part of Lost society because it offers some level of reassurance in the face of exactly this sort of difficulty in extending trust in the world touch by the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}